Top Docker Commands Every DevOps Engineer Should Know 🐳
🔧 Most Used Docker Commands:

docker ps – List running containers
📘 Docs - https://lnkd.in/gizyukqC

docker images – List all images on your system
📘 Docs - https://lnkd.in/gFTJ4r2J

docker run – Run a command in a new container
📘 Docs - https://lnkd.in/ghrBm3Rk

docker exec – Execute a command in a running container
📘 Docs - https://lnkd.in/gb4eYpPH

docker logs – View logs from a container
📘 Docs - https://lnkd.in/gf5aVmEJ

docker build – Build an image from a Dockerfile
📘 Docs - https://lnkd.in/gTUswrX4

docker stop / docker start – Manage container lifecycle
📘 Stop | Start - https://lnkd.in/gasjetEd

docker rm / docker rmi – Remove containers or images
📘 rm | rmi - https://lnkd.in/g2FGcSkH

docker-compose up – Start services defined in docker-compose.yml
📘 Docs - https://lnkd.in/g5BstjaZ

docker network ls – List Docker networks
📘 Docs - https://lnkd.in/gJknH-73
